Antivirus (AV)
AVs are often misunderstood as a blanket protection measure, but they are primarily 
made to safeguard endpoints, such as desktops, laptops, and servers, from known malicious 
files and programs. Most AVs rely on signature-based detection, which means they compare 
files with a database of known malware or patterns.